# Production deploy (decksy.ru)

After completing user-requested fixes or features that touch the app, **deploy to production yourself** without asking the user to run commands manually.

## Server

- Host: `159.194.221.146` (`root`, path `/var/www/decksy`)
- Domain: https://decksy.ru
- Process: PM2 `decksy` on port 3000
- Do **not** break coexisting services (loopera on :5001, loopera-postgres on :5432)

## Workflow

1. Ensure changes are committed and pushed to `origin/main` (commit only when the user asked or deploy implies shipping their work).
2. Run from repo root:

```bash
chmod +x scripts/deploy-prod.sh
./scripts/deploy-prod.sh
```

Credentials live in gitignored `.env.deploy` (`SSHPASS`). Never commit secrets.

## When to deploy

- User says "задеплой", "deploy", "на прод", or "always deploy yourself"
- After finishing a feature/bugfix the user expects on decksy.ru
- Skip deploy for question-only or local-only experiments unless asked

## Verify

- `https://decksy.ru/` returns HTTP 200
- PM2 status `decksy` is `online`
- Server HEAD matches latest git commit on main
